"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/events/402018221","actor":{"login":"nzakas","id":38546,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas","html_url":"https://github.com/nzakas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2015-09-06T00:49:57Z","label":{"name":"accepted","color":"0052cc"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":402018222,"node_id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50NDAyMDE4MjIy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/events/402018222","actor":{"login":"nzakas","id":38546,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas","html_url":"https://github.com/nzakas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"unlabeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2015-09-06T00:49:57Z","label":{"name":"triage","color":"cc317c"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":402018261,"node_id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50NDAyMDE4MjYx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/events/402018261","actor":{"login":"nzakas","id":38546,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas","html_url":"https://github.com/nzakas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"renamed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2015-09-06T00:50:23Z","rename":{"from":"Rule Proposal: no-arrow-bind","to":"Update no-extra-bind docs to mention arrow function"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/138043844","html_url":"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/3672#issuecomment-138043844","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/3672","id":138043844,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDEzODA0Mzg0NA==","user":{"login":"solmsted","id":651608,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MTYwOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/651608?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted","html_url":"https://github.com/solmsted","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-09-06T05:58:15Z","updated_at":"2015-09-06T05:58:15Z","body":"I could be mistaken but if I understand you correctly, I feel like the implementation of `no-extra-bind` is incomplete.  Here are some tests I ran.  All of these used version 1.3.1 and this .eslintrc:\n\n```\n{\n    \"ecmaFeatures\": {\n        \"modules\": true\n    },\n    \"env\": {\n        \"es6\": true\n    },\n    \"root\": true,\n    \"rules\": {\n        \"no-extra-bind\": 2\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe basic check as described in the docs warns as expected:\n\n```\nconst someFunction = function () {}.bind('something');\n```\n\n`1:22  error  The function binding is unnecessary  no-extra-bind`\n\nAs you pointed out, it warns as expected with arrow functions too:\n\n```\nconst someFunction = (() => {}).bind('something');\n```\n\n`1:22  error  The function binding is unnecessary  no-extra-bind`\n\nIt does not warn if the arrow function's body contains `this`:\n\n```\nconst someFunction = (() => {return this;}).bind('something');\n```\n\nNo warning.  My proposal was intended to address this.  It seems like `someFunction` should always return `'something'` but it will instead return whatever the `this` value happens to be in the parent scope.\n\nI discovered that there is no warning if you call bind on a variable instead of directly on the function expression:\n\n```\nconst someFunction = function () {},\n    someBoundFunction = someFunction.bind('something');\n```\n\nNo warning.  This wasn't part of my original proposal but I feel like this is a more common pattern and it should generate a `no-extra-bind` warning.  I realize it's not always possible to statically determine the value of a variable but it should be possible in some cases.\n\nUsing `Function.prototype.call`:\n\n```\nconst someValue = function (arg) {return arg;}.call('something', 'someValue');\n```\n\nNo warning.\n\nUsing `Function.prototype.apply`:\n\n```\nconst someValue = function (arg) {return arg;}.apply('something', [\n    'someValue'\n]);\n```\n\nNo warning.\n\nUsing `Reflect.apply`:\n\n```\nconst someValue = Reflect.apply(function (arg) {return arg;}, 'something', [\n    'someValue'\n]);\n```\n\nNo warning.\n\nSo in summary, I'd like to request a few enhancements.\n- Instead of just checking `Function.prototype.bind`, check for all mechanisms that could change the `this` value.\n  - There's a dilemma I mentioned originally.  Other functions like `Function.prototype.call` are still perfectly valid for specifying arguments so warnings should only be generated when obviously attempting to set the thisArgument.\n- Instead of just checking function expressions also check for extra bindings when the function has been saved to a variable (where possible)\n- Instead of just checking functions that don't use `this` also check for arrow functions that contain `this` which can not be rebound.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/138043844/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"solmsted","id":651608,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MTYwOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/651608?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted","html_url":"https://github.com/solmsted","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solmsted/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/138098254","html_url":"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/3672#issuecomment-138098254","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/3672","id":138098254,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDEzODA5ODI1NA==","user":{"login":"nzakas","id":38546,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas","html_url":"https://github.com/nzakas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-09-06T16:37:37Z","updated_at":"2015-09-06T16:37:37Z","body":"> I realize it's not always possible to statically determine the value of a variable but it should be possible in some cases.\n\nWe don't ever do this, it's too dangerous to check in some cases but not others. It also sets expectations poorly for how ESLint works.\n\n> Instead of just checking Function.prototype.bind, check for all mechanisms that could change the this value.\n\nIf we did this, it would be a separate rule. That said, I don't see this as the same as `bind`, so I'm not sure such a rule would be useful. Unlike `bind`, the other methods don't create a new function so there's less occasion for trouble. \n\n> Instead of just checking function expressions also check for extra bindings when the function has been saved to a variable (where possible)\n\nAs already mentioned, we do not track variable values, so we don't do these sorts of checks.\n\n> Instead of just checking functions that don't use this also check for arrow functions that contain this which can not be rebound.\n\nI think this is an actual bug we should fix.\n\n---\n\nKeep in mind, you can always create your own rules that do what you want even if we don't want it in core, so you have options for achieving what you want.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/138098254/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"nzakas","id":38546,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas","html_url":"https://github.com/nzakas","followers_url":"http